bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:currentRecord bcoc:record-f8620a7e33a23e5f5dca2173b16e796303e172ec0cb3487e47c615fa20f0c037 .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:definitionGenus bco:BusinessCapability .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:foundationalAncestor cco:ont00000568 .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:lifecycleStatus "Draft" .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-3c7c642f5a0179876a5d092352483f454291c7d88136fc6870216096fdac53bc .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-7fbc3e395fbf7b5de65a40d2ae8efb38bd86a1bbd43695fb0d7bf146cb9ae03a .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-aa18f2be9785bc5958d0fc79b9b3d3c15742ece3e290f43d0435a829edd67a81 .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance dcterms:created "2026-10-24T12:14:15+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance prov:wasAttributedTo bcoa:claude-opus-5-5 .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance rdf:type skos:Concept .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance skos:changeNote "2026-10-24, review R6 section 3.1: generalized, and the development clause removed. The definition said that acts first establishing this oversight develop the capability and are not, on that ground alone, realizations of it. That is specification CD5's distinction between developing and realizing a capability, and it is stated there for every capability; restating it in one definition made it read as a condition peculiar to this one. The definition now says what the capability is for. \"Realized in\" became \"realizable in\" (CD8). Every source is now marked contextual (R6 section 6.1)."@en .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance skos:changeNote "2026-10-25, review R7 section 4: \"decides how they should change\" became \"decides whether and how they should change\", so that deciding to change nothing is a realization of the capability too. The genus field now names the immediate genus, bco:BusinessCapability: the class the definition's text names and bcom:BusinessCapability designates. cco:ont00000568 (Organization Capability) moved to foundational_ancestor (review R7 Finding E; docs/decisions/2026-10-25-r7-genus-decision.md). Nothing is minted."@en .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance skos:definition "A business capability, inhering in an organization, that is realizable in planned acts by which that organization judges whether the business models it operates by still serve it, and decides whether and how they should change."@en .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance skos:inScheme bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance skos:prefLabel "Business Model Governance"@en .

bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme rdf:type skos:ConceptScheme .
bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme skos:definition "The business capabilities the BCO catalogues."@en .
bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme skos:prefLabel "BCO capability catalog scheme"@en .

bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis bco:currentRecord bcoc:record-657667441ade80f7950cc6bd8f8d55e4dfe07aef0cd41ac7427ae48a9ce02413 .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis bco:definitionGenus bco:BusinessCapability .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis bco:foundationalAncestor cco:ont00000568 .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis bco:lifecycleStatus "Draft" .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-12523d5f190ddcc954ccbf335a2ff64ec7e1e12da0c3a15007e1b923cb04bdba .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-7fbc3e395fbf7b5de65a40d2ae8efb38bd86a1bbd43695fb0d7bf146cb9ae03a .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-aa18f2be9785bc5958d0fc79b9b3d3c15742ece3e290f43d0435a829edd67a81 .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis dcterms:created "2026-10-24T12:14:15+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis prov:wasAttributedTo bcoa:claude-opus-5-5 .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis rdf:type skos:Concept .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis skos:changeNote "2026-10-24, review R6 section 3.2: generalized, and a clause dropped. The definition required the analysis to be carried out through coordinated work among the organization's members, not resting on one analyst's skill. That made the number of members doing the work part of what the capability is, which specification CD2's \"Fragility is not reclassification\" bullet denies: a capability may depend on one indispensable member and still be the organization's. Whether capabilities of this type are organizational rather than a person's Skill is asked once, at type admission (G1-T question 3), not stated as a condition on every instance. \"Realized in\" became \"realizable in\" (CD8). Every source is now marked contextual (R6 section 6.1)."@en .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis skos:changeNote "2026-10-25, review R7 section 4: \"organizations\" became \"agents\". A competitor need not be an organization: a sole trader is a person. The bearer of the capability is still an organization; only what it analyses is widened. The genus field now names the immediate genus, bco:BusinessCapability: the class the definition's text names and bcom:BusinessCapability designates. cco:ont00000568 (Organization Capability) moved to foundational_ancestor (review R7 Finding E; docs/decisions/2026-10-25-r7-genus-decision.md). Nothing is minted."@en .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis skos:definition "A business capability, inhering in an organization, that is realizable in planned acts by which that organization gathers and interprets information about the agents it competes with, or may come to compete with, to inform its own decisions."@en .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis skos:inScheme bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme .
bcoc:CompetitiveAnalysis skos:prefLabel "Competitive Analysis"@en .

bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement bco:currentRecord bcoc:record-1f8db5fa47c5c09802d00dc51673e0c8edbd0be187c025471205634d8ad7fc73 .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement bco:definitionGenus bco:BusinessCapability .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement bco:foundationalAncestor cco:ont00000568 .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement bco:lifecycleStatus "Draft" .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-3c7c642f5a0179876a5d092352483f454291c7d88136fc6870216096fdac53bc .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-7fbc3e395fbf7b5de65a40d2ae8efb38bd86a1bbd43695fb0d7bf146cb9ae03a .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-aa18f2be9785bc5958d0fc79b9b3d3c15742ece3e290f43d0435a829edd67a81 .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement dcterms:created "2026-10-24T12:14:15+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement prov:wasAttributedTo bcoa:claude-opus-5-5 .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement rdf:type skos:Concept .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement skos:changeNote "2026-10-24, review R6 section 3.3: generalized. The definition required the organization to appraise its customers' experience, set a strategy for it, and design customer interactions and their supporting structures, all three. An organization that manages its customers' experience well without a separately stated strategy would have been excluded. It now says what the capability is for. \"Realized in\" became \"realizable in\" (CD8). Every source is now marked contextual (R6 section 6.1)."@en .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement skos:changeNote "2026-10-25, review R7 section 4: \"comes to understand, and acts to shape\" became \"understands or shapes\". The definition names the kinds of planned act the capability is realizable in, and an act of either kind realizes it. Reading the conjunction as requiring both repeated the problem R6 section 3 removed: listed practices read as conditions that must all hold, which would deny the capability to an organization able to do only one of the two. The cost, stated: an organization that only studies its customers' experience now has the capability. That is the reading chosen; the architect may reverse it. The genus field now names the immediate genus, bco:BusinessCapability: the class the definition's text names and bcom:BusinessCapability designates. cco:ont00000568 (Organization Capability) moved to foundational_ancestor (review R7 Finding E; docs/decisions/2026-10-25-r7-genus-decision.md). Nothing is minted."@en .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement skos:definition "A business capability, inhering in an organization, that is realizable in planned acts by which that organization understands or shapes the experience its customers have in their dealings with it."@en .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement skos:inScheme bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme .
bcoc:CustomerExperienceManagement skos:prefLabel "Customer Experience Management"@en .

bcoc:StrategicPlanning bco:currentRecord bcoc:record-be402280b2f3b07028701f2587b48052a6eba818267a49ef2346cec616044b96 .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning bco:definitionGenus bco:BusinessCapability .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning bco:foundationalAncestor cco:ont00000568 .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning bco:lifecycleStatus "Draft" .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-31186a3c539c44bac2327592126f17c6e1915d4c03329d94684e77516cd1e6e1 .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-3c7c642f5a0179876a5d092352483f454291c7d88136fc6870216096fdac53bc .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-7fbc3e395fbf7b5de65a40d2ae8efb38bd86a1bbd43695fb0d7bf146cb9ae03a .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-aa18f2be9785bc5958d0fc79b9b3d3c15742ece3e290f43d0435a829edd67a81 .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning dcterms:created "2026-10-24T12:14:15+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning prov:wasAttributedTo bcoa:claude-opus-5-5 .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning rdf:type skos:Concept .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:changeNote "2026-10-24, review R6 section 3.4: generalized. The definition named a mission statement, a long-term strategic vision, and enterprise-wide and business-unit strategies. An organization with no business units or no written mission can still plan strategically, so the list made customary practices necessary conditions. It now says what the capability is for. \"Realized in\" became \"realizable in\" (CD8). Every source is now marked contextual (R6 section 6.1)."@en .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:changeNote "2026-10-25, review R7 section 4: \"long-range\" dropped. Planning over a short horizon, or revising aims in response to an event, can be strategic, and the qualifier excluded it. The genus field now names the immediate genus, bco:BusinessCapability: the class the definition's text names and bcom:BusinessCapability designates. cco:ont00000568 (Organization Capability) moved to foundational_ancestor (review R7 Finding E; docs/decisions/2026-10-25-r7-genus-decision.md). Nothing is minted."@en .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:definition "A business capability, inhering in an organization, that is realizable in planned acts by which that organization sets or revises its aims and the courses of action it means to take toward them."@en .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:inScheme bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:prefLabel "Strategic Planning"@en .

bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:currentRecord bcoc:record-1670739b1e9d40900ef0f391c304b9dbd25adeb081314959bf2b3674f811e3ae .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:definitionGenus bco:BusinessCapability .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:foundationalAncestor cco:ont00000568 .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:lifecycleStatus "Draft" .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-3c7c642f5a0179876a5d092352483f454291c7d88136fc6870216096fdac53bc .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-7fbc3e395fbf7b5de65a40d2ae8efb38bd86a1bbd43695fb0d7bf146cb9ae03a .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-aa18f2be9785bc5958d0fc79b9b3d3c15742ece3e290f43d0435a829edd67a81 .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement dcterms:created "2026-10-24T12:14:15+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement prov:wasAttributedTo bcoa:claude-opus-5-5 .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement rdf:type skos:Concept .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:changeNote "2026-10-24, review R6 section 3.5: generalized. The definition required treasury oversight, cash tracking and reconciliation, an investment policy and a hedging strategy, all four. A small business that manages its liquidity without hedging would have been excluded. It now says what the capability is for: having the means to pay when payment falls due. \"Realized in\" became \"realizable in\" (CD8). Every source is now marked contextual (R6 section 6.1)."@en .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:changeNote "2026-10-25, review R7 section 4: \"ensures\" removed. It made a successful outcome, always having the cash to pay, a condition of having the capability, so an organization that manages its liquidity and still meets a funding shortfall would not have it. The capability is an ability to undertake the management; the definition now says what that management is directed toward. The wording follows the reviewer's suggested refinement in substance. The genus field now names the immediate genus, bco:BusinessCapability: the class the definition's text names and bcom:BusinessCapability designates. cco:ont00000568 (Organization Capability) moved to foundational_ancestor (review R7 Finding E; docs/decisions/2026-10-25-r7-genus-decision.md). Nothing is minted."@en .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:definition "A business capability, inhering in an organization, that is realizable in planned acts by which that organization manages its cash positions, liquidity, funding and financial exposures toward meeting its financial obligations."@en .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:inScheme bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:prefLabel "Treasury Management"@en .

